emains a local question.','Progress flow-control variants and malformed input behavior require separate bounded questions.'])\ncore['formation']=dict(explanation='A caller proposes through RawNode or Node.run. Followers may forward; leaders reject proposals during transfer/removal or quota exhaustion. Accepted entries get leader term and consecutive index, enter unstable log and generate deferred self append support. Replication carries preceding index/term, entries and commit. Followers match the preceding entry, refuse committed conflicts, append only the conflicting suffix and acknowledge through the resulting prefix; stale prefixes can acknowledge the existing committed boundary. Ready or asynchronous local append envelopes impose the storage-before-response contract. Successful current-term tracked replies update per-peer Match. The active voter majority order statistic, minimum across both joint halves, supplies a candidate commit index; raftLog advances only when its entry term matches current leader term. Append broadcasts and bounded heartbeat commit propagate the decision. Ready then supplies committed entries, with asynchronous application restricted to locally stable entries and snapshots blocking entry application. Advance or apply response reports completion; the caller owns actual state-machine effects and client acknowledgement. Propose success alone is not commitment.',behavior_ids=['B-entry','B-propose','B-follower-append','B-storage-release','B-aggregate','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-app-queued','F-match','F-committed','F-apply-reported'],source_ids=['entry','leader-admit','candidate-follower','send-replication','append-receive','log-start-append','reply-queue','async-contract','leader-match','tracker-commit','majority','joint','log-eligibility','log-apply','ready-contract','node-loop'])\ncore['context']=dict(explanation='Election ticks or Campaign pass eligibility and unapplied-configuration guards. PreVote collects support without changing term/vote;